# Stripe (Wawona + Cursor)

When the user mentions Stripe, Checkout, donations, invoicing, Ko-fi vs Stripe,
publishable/secret keys, or `mcp.stripe.com`:

1. Read `~/.cursor/skills/stripe-best-practices/SKILL.md` and its
   `references/payments.md`, `billing.md`, `security.md`.
2. Read `~/.cursor/skills/stripe-wawona/SKILL.md` for this machine's pass/SecretSpec paths.
3. Prefer Stripe MCP (`stripe_implementation_planner`, `stripe_api_write`) when authenticated.
   Skills also live in `~/.cursor/plugins/local/stripe` (nix-darwin `modules/apps/stripe.nix`).
4. Never write `sk_` / `rk_` into the repo. Publishable `pk_` keys may live in `config.toml`.
5. Ko-fi is a hosted donation page + webhooks, not a Checkout Session API.
